data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":1470,"item_id":"msg_0bb7a255fed21794016b09ece42fe087d1a1ff57ef2308c1e7","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"queries\":[],\"result_json\":\"{\\\"reviews\\\":[{\\\"actor\\\":\\\"lin\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"develop\\\",\\\"ability\\\":null,\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Develop a general mechanical food-processing operation through the current-conversation handoff. Related capabilities have been searched. probe supports observation and a consumptive press test, but its documented modes do not implement peeling, cutting, shell fracture or conserved processing products. The existing hazelnut press finding establishes only that a 0.2 load was held without flexibility, not that the shell can be opened. unheated-food-preparation only dry-brushes whole units; it is not equivalent. The retrieved candidates are incomplete, so absence of any other equivalent is not established: the handoff must check the remaining related registry contracts before adding code and use any equivalent implementation and its existing learning duration instead. Missing physical mechanisms warrant development, not permanent rejection or a claim that these particular foods can already be processed.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"General operation: Mechanical food separation. Parameters: exact owned inputStackId, quantity in supported inventory increments, mode inspect or trial, operation open/peel/cut, optional exact implementId and supportId, and progress/resume/cancel modes. Any applicable actor may learn it. Implement the smallest supported hands-on separation trial, not tool manufacture, cooking or a sequence of future unlocks. Reuse existing ownership, reach, inventory splitting, ageing, observations and event machinery, recording exact reused handlers and revisions; record probe/open.probe/foundation-open@1 as an existing comparison, not a newly invented press test. Do not assume its press output implements fracture.\\\\nCurrent references: lin owns item-180-lin-2343, quantity 2 roots, and item-19-lin-197, quantity 0.9 hazelnut. Recheck their live condition and location; old inspection records are not current safety tests. No implement, water, fire, vessel or suitable support has been established. Source plants are not owned supplies. Do not spawn equipment, replacement food or knowledge. Do not round 0.9 hazelnut into a whole nut or infer its geometry from the resource name; determine whether that remainder has represented processable structure. Whole-shell opening requires an actual intact shell; a suitable fragment may instead support an applicable separation trial.\\\\nHandoff must supply an executable material/contact kernel before activation: represented geometry, accessible edges/layers or shell, grip/support requirements, bounded hand or implement force and work, separation/fracture resistance, and product allocation. Use authoritative implementation properties without disclosing hidden values to the actor. Do not derive these properties or edibility from names or arbitrary success rolls. If the needed properties are absent, implement their minimal supported representation in this handoff, explicitly documenting model assumptions and provenance rather than calling them discoveries. Until a separation rule is supported, the executable precursor is an observation or bounded contact attempt reporting unknown/not established, never a successful opening. A cutting action requires an actually acquired suitable edge and support; hand peeling requires a represented accessible separable layer; hand opening requires a represented shell and force within hand capacity. No teeth-based ingestion, forced injury or automatic equipment acquisition.\\\\nCosts: proposed study 3 rounds at 0.2 energy each, individually paid by each learner. inspect or inspect-progress costs 1 round and 0.2 energy, using no food. A supported trial consists of one setup round at 0.2 energy and one bounded working round at 0.5 energy; quantity selects at most one processable unit or represented fragment per bout. The kernel must publish its force/work limit and implement wear or breakage costs before execution. Unsupported modes, missing ownership/reach/means, invalid quantities and insufficient energy refuse before charging; an actual paid observation/contact that finds uncertainty or resistance remains a completed observation/contact, not a processing success. No arbitrary mandatory food destruction: loss occurs only through modeled separation, damage, spillage or wear. Additional bouts require fresh checks and their own costs.\\\\nSetup reserves the selected quantity without copying or consuming it. Store exact item/version, quantity, chosen operation, means, completed paid phase and any actual partial damage. Each working phase atomically debits the input portion and creates only physically supported products: retained food portions, detached peel/shell, fragments and accounted unrecoverable debris, with explicit conversion and a material ledger. Total material cannot increase; implement loss must also be accounted for. If the inventory cannot represent these outputs, extend it minimally before enabling separation rather than rounding or creating stock. Preserve origin, age, decay, contamination and unknown safety; distribute existing nutritional contents without multiplying them. Do not count shell or peel as edible merely because its parent stack was food. Failed contact may leave the input unchanged or actually damaged as the kernel determines. No identification, detoxification, improved nutrition, preservation, safety certification or feeding follows from this action.\\\\nAnother action, loss of reach, low energy or unavailable means pauses before further charges; resume revalidates the exact input, current damage and means and performs only unpaid work. Changed or missing inputs invalidate outstanding reservations. Cancel costs one round and no energy, releases unchanged reserved material once and retains all real products, damage and expenditure. Death stops work, clears reservations once and leaves material/products under ordinary death and ownership rules. No time, energy, lost material or wear refunds; no undo of completed changes. Products continue ordinary ageing; there is no autonomous processing, special maintenance or passive benefit. Inspection never freezes decay. Work and study advance time only on actual paid simulation actions; review/development waiting does not. All eligibility, charging, conservation, progress and outcome rules execute in code, not repeated model adjudication.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":3,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"No experience benefit for requesting, registration, study, naming, queries or mastery. This request explicitly seeks no happiness award, so the minimal implementation adds none. Existing verified-information rules may independently recognize a genuinely new measured response, including informative failure, only if applicable to lin and supported by an actual event; consult or repeated inspection alone is insufficient. Such recognition must use existing functional deduplication, bounded per-event and aggregate caps, cooldown and decay, with no stacking of equivalent observations. Do not invent those bounds or modify protected reward accounts, budgets, goals or permissions. No pleasure, comfort, satisfaction or nutrition increase follows merely from a successful separation; any later eating uses the ordinary nutrition rules without mood reduction. Any future physical comfort remains capped at 10.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Implement reusable event metadata for mechanical-food-separation: actor, exact input/output ids, operation, means, location, paid phase, observable contact, visible damage/separation, outcome and failure reason, with no hidden material constants. Show setup and hand/tool contact only when performed. Render shell pieces, peel, exposed surfaces or cut portions only when those products actually exist; unknown or resisted attempts show unresolved contact or no visible change, not an opened-food success icon. Distinguish paused, cancelled, unsupported, damaged and completed outcomes. Events should support other actors' ordinary observation without revealing safety, nutrition or unobserved properties. Visual appeal is separate from functional processing and supplies no automatic experience reward.\\\"}]}\"}","logprobs":[]}

